# Benchmark output files
benchmark_output.txt
benchmark_run*.txt
benchmark_*_results.json
benchmark_results_*.json
*_benchmark_output.txt
thorough_benchmark_output.txt
# Root-level dated transport captures (bench_nda_2026-09-17.txt,
# bench_results_core5.txt, bench_comprehensive_*, bench_nda_run, …). Repo policy is
# that raw benchmark output stays a local artifact, but these sat in the gap between
# "tracked" and "ignored" — which is how the bench_nda/ copies got committed by
# accident. Anchored with a leading slash so bench_nda/*.txt keeps its own rule.
# Docs cite these files as run provenance; the durable record is the tables in the
# docs, regenerable with `cargo run --release --manifest-path bench_nda/Cargo.toml`.
/bench_*.txt
# bench_nda's own raw captures. Five such files were committed before this rule
# existed and stay tracked until someone runs `git rm --cached` on them; nothing
# new matching these patterns should be added.
bench_nda/*.txt
bench_nda/audit_*.json

# Coverage artifacts
*.profraw

# Test fixture directories
test_nda_dir/
test_registry_list_dir/
test_registry_search/
test_registry_tree/
test_registry_*.txt

# Temp build intermediates
*.o.tmp
bench_tools/r_wasm/webr.wasm
bench_tools/webr.wasm

# WASIX build artifacts (built locally via cargo-wasix, not committed)
crates/velocity-mcp-edge/velocity-edge-wasix.wasm

# Nested-WASM PoC build artifact (rebuild via deploy/build-edge-poc.py)
nested-poc/poc.wasm
crates/velocity-mcp-edge/velocity-edge.wasm
# Python editable-install metadata written in-tree by "pip install -e ." (regenerated on demand)
*.egg-info/
# Python bytecode caches written in-tree by importing the SDK package
__pycache__/
*.pyc
